From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Bluetooth: hci_qca: support the Piano Brahma controller

Carry the controller firmware, UART and power sequencing changes for Piano.

The port retains changes from these linux-piano commits:
piano: bt/geni: speed override and UART clock-choice markers (bring-up) (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: bt: piano_retries module parameter; drop the SE clock table dump (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
BACKPORT-ELDEN: wifi/bt/pwrseq: Peach v2 (WCN7861) support from the Lenovo Y700 Gen4 port (GEEKiDoS <geek_ds@foxmail.com>)
piano: bt: btqca: log the controller board ID (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: bt: hci_qca: patch the Brahma PERI subsystem before the BT rampatch (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: bt: hci_qca: wake BT and re-read its version after PERI activation (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)
piano: bt: hci_qca: move the Brahma UART to 8 Mbaud through PERI (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)

Co-authored-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: GEEKiDoS <geek_ds@foxmail.com>

